WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.268
-I'm so excited that everybody
is going to see this special.

00:00:02.268 --> 00:00:04.270
I saw one of the -- You did
seven shows at Radio City.

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:06.072 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was lucky enough to be
at one of them.

00:00:06.072 --> 00:00:06.706 size:88% position:44% line:92%
It's an incredible hour.

00:00:06.706 --> 00:00:08.241 size:84% position:42%
And you just wrapped up
your tour last night

00:00:08.241 --> 00:00:10.076 line:92%
in Jacksonville, Florida.

00:00:10.076 --> 00:00:10.477 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:00:10.477 --> 00:00:12.645 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's been about a solid year
from the last May

00:00:12.645 --> 00:00:15.048 align:start size:94% position:6%
in Portland, Maine,
to Jacksonville, Florida.

00:00:15.048 --> 00:00:17.250 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's great.
-The opposite of Maine.

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:18.418 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Absolutely.
-Absolutely.

00:00:18.418 --> 00:00:20.487 size:75% position:38%
And we did a show at
the Florida theater.

00:00:20.487 --> 00:00:22.956 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that's the end of
the "Kid Gorgeous" tour.

00:00:22.956 --> 00:00:24.724 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Congratulations on that.
-Thank you.

00:00:24.724 --> 00:00:27.093
-I heard that
someone asked you why comedians

00:00:27.093 --> 00:00:30.096 align:start size:94% position:6%
make fun of Florida
when you were in Florida.

00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:30.530 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:32.565 align:start size:94% position:6%
I met a very nice young woman,
16-year-old girl,

00:00:32.565 --> 00:00:33.700 line:92%
came up to me after the show.

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:35.902 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she said, "I want to be
a comedy writer.

00:00:35.902 --> 00:00:36.703 line:92%
I want to write at 'SNL.'"

00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:38.571 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I said,
"I used to write there."

00:00:38.571 --> 00:00:39.272 size:81% position:41% line:92%
And she said, "I know.

00:00:39.272 --> 00:00:40.573 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's why I'm talking to you
about it."

00:00:40.573 --> 00:00:44.778
She said, "why do comedians
always go after Florida?"

00:00:44.778 --> 00:00:47.747 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like,
"Huh, that's a good point."

00:00:47.747 --> 00:00:48.281 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:48.281 --> 00:00:50.150 align:start size:94% position:6%
"We kind of do."
She's like, "Yes, you do."

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:52.185 size:81% position:41%
She said, "There was
a Jeremy Renner sketch

00:00:52.185 --> 00:00:55.422
when he hosted 'SNL' where he
played the mayor of Tampa."

00:00:55.422 --> 00:00:58.124 align:start size:94% position:6%
"And when he said,
'I'm the mayor of Tampa,'

00:00:58.124 --> 00:00:59.993 line:92%
everyone laughed automatically."

00:00:59.993 --> 00:01:00.593 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.593 --> 00:01:01.961 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I said to her like --
I said,

00:01:01.961 --> 00:01:05.465 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Well, it's not fair
that we laugh at Florida."

00:01:05.465 --> 00:01:07.434 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said, "Comedy writers
are often lazy.

00:01:07.434 --> 00:01:10.170
And so it's like a good example
of a place when you need --"

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:12.972
you know, if you had a lot of
paper towels, I'd be like,

00:01:12.972 --> 00:01:15.275
"Hey, Seth,
what are you, Costco?" You know?

00:01:15.275 --> 00:01:16.843 align:start size:94% position:6%
Not a good joke.
Not a good joke.

00:01:16.843 --> 00:01:18.378 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it's easy, right?
-Yeah.

00:01:18.378 --> 00:01:18.912 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:18.912 --> 00:01:23.516
-So Florida is the Costco of
upsetting people, you know?

00:01:23.516 --> 00:01:24.117 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:24.117 --> 00:01:26.586 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, it's just everything
at once.

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:29.155 align:start size:94% position:6%
You'd never make Florida
on purpose.

00:01:29.155 --> 00:01:31.958 align:start size:94% position:6%
You'd never put it together,
like --

00:01:31.958 --> 00:01:33.359 line:92%
like if it was a dinner party,

00:01:33.359 --> 00:01:37.864
you wouldn't be like, "Hey, you
know who we should invite?

00:01:37.864 --> 00:01:39.232 line:92%
A bunch of elderly Jewish people

00:01:39.232 --> 00:01:42.335
and some really cool gay people
from South Beach,

00:01:42.335 --> 00:01:44.170 align:start size:94% position:6%
and a bunch of
conservative Cubans

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:47.640 align:start size:94% position:6%
and a woman that looks like
Bret 'The Hitman' Hart

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:48.274 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
driving a fan boat

00:01:48.274 --> 00:01:54.280 align:start size:94% position:6%
and a possum and an alligator
and 12 serial killers

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:58.318
and the richest people in the
world trying not to pay taxes."

00:01:58.318 --> 00:02:00.453 align:start size:94% position:6%
And at the end of
the dinner party,

00:02:00.453 --> 00:02:02.355 align:start size:94% position:6%
they decide
who the president is.

00:02:02.355 --> 00:02:05.458 size:81% position:41%
You wouldn't form it.
-You wouldn't form it.

00:02:05.458 --> 00:02:07.227 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:07.227 --> 00:02:08.962 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-But I love Florida.

00:02:08.962 --> 00:02:10.196 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:10.196 --> 00:02:10.597 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, wow.

00:02:10.597 --> 00:02:13.867 align:start size:94% position:6%
I see what you did there.
-You see what I did?

00:02:13.867 --> 00:02:16.803 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You got out of it.
-Restored goodwill.

00:02:16.803 --> 00:02:20.507 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You mentioned they decide
who the president is.

00:02:20.507 --> 00:02:25.211
Are you surprised that espionage
might be the thing

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:27.013 align:start size:94% position:6%
that brings down
the Trump presidency?

00:02:27.013 --> 00:02:28.248 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's the weirdest thing
to me.

00:02:28.248 --> 00:02:30.650 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is that like -- I don't follow
the news that well,

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:32.785 align:start size:94% position:6%
but there's a Russia thing
or whatever.

00:02:32.785 --> 00:02:34.554 line:92%
Like, if you told me like,

00:02:34.554 --> 00:02:36.523 size:78% position:39%
"Oh, why do you think
the game show host

00:02:36.523 --> 00:02:38.858
who accidentally became
president got impeached?"

00:02:38.858 --> 00:02:41.394 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'd be like, "I don't know,
just 'cause?" You know?

00:02:41.394 --> 00:02:44.230 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'd never think, like, it was
high-stakes espionage.

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:46.232 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's like if
they arrested Godzilla.

00:02:46.232 --> 00:02:47.700 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's like,
"We got Godzilla."

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:50.670
And it's like, "Oh, for burning
down the city?"

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:52.038 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Like, "No, tax evasion."

00:02:52.038 --> 00:02:53.506 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:53.506 --> 00:02:56.976
He said his -- his apartment was
his office.

00:02:56.976 --> 00:02:57.510 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:57.510 --> 00:03:01.347
I shouldn't have said that.
I did that. That's not good.

00:03:01.347 --> 00:03:02.415 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-That's how you know.

00:03:02.415 --> 00:03:05.018 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I work out of
my apartment.

00:03:05.018 --> 00:03:06.286 line:92%
-We used to work together,

00:03:06.286 --> 00:03:08.655 size:88% position:44%
as that 16-year-old girl
in Florida pointed out.

00:03:08.655 --> 00:03:09.422 line:92%
We were on "SNL" together.

00:03:09.422 --> 00:03:11.524
And you hosted, congratulations,
such a great episode.

00:03:11.524 --> 00:03:12.926 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, thank you.
That was very, very fun.

00:03:12.926 --> 00:03:15.695 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheers and applause ]
-I was so excited to watch.

00:03:15.695 --> 00:03:20.733 align:start size:94% position:6%
You posted a photo of
when Jon Hamm hosted "SNL."

00:03:20.733 --> 00:03:21.201 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:03:21.201 --> 00:03:25.438 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We all dressed up
like "Mad Men"-era writers.

00:03:25.438 --> 00:03:25.872 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:03:25.872 --> 00:03:28.041 line:92%
-And we got drunk in the day.

00:03:28.041 --> 00:03:30.510 align:start size:94% position:6%
-All of you did. I didn't.
-Yeah.

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:34.948 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then we went in
to pitch dressed like this.

00:03:34.948 --> 00:03:36.082 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Which is normally like --
pitch,

00:03:36.082 --> 00:03:39.452
I would say is a mundane meeting
at the end of Monday.

00:03:39.452 --> 00:03:40.119 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Everyone's pretty tired.

00:03:40.119 --> 00:03:42.855
It's normally, kind of, all
business and a little fun.

00:03:42.855 --> 00:03:46.392
And we got fully dressed up
as "Mad Men" characters.

00:03:46.392 --> 00:03:47.594 line:92%
A lot of people forgot to do it,

00:03:47.594 --> 00:03:52.932
and so they threw together like
pieces of wigs and dresses.

00:03:52.932 --> 00:03:54.867 line:92%
Marika Sawyer just had a tie.

00:03:54.867 --> 00:03:59.305 align:start size:94% position:6%
We were all smoking
and showed up to pitch drunk,

00:03:59.305 --> 00:04:02.609 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Jon Hamm is there
for his first time ever.

00:04:02.609 --> 00:04:03.042 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:04:03.042 --> 00:04:05.578
-Like, and it was like
Comic-Con, but alcoholic.

00:04:05.578 --> 00:04:06.112 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:06.112 --> 00:04:08.648
-Also, Jon Hamm was dressed like
modern-day Jon Hamm.

00:04:08.648 --> 00:04:10.917 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Exactly.
-Which was very jarring to us,

00:04:10.917 --> 00:04:12.418 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause we knew him
as Don Draper,

00:04:12.418 --> 00:04:15.655
and he was wearing like
a St. Louis Blues baseball hat.

00:04:15.655 --> 00:04:17.423 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, he was dressed
like a person.

00:04:17.423 --> 00:04:20.560 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we were like, "Oh, you're
not 'Mad Men' like us."

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:21.094 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:21.094 --> 00:04:23.162 align:start size:94% position:6%
-A lot of attention has been
paid for you outing

00:04:23.162 --> 00:04:25.331 align:start size:94% position:6%
how Colin Jost used to look,
with that weird...

00:04:25.331 --> 00:04:27.166 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Was that a secret
that Jost had a beard?

00:04:27.166 --> 00:04:28.568 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I don't know.
-I never knew that.

00:04:28.568 --> 00:04:30.370 align:start size:94% position:6%
He had long hair and a beard
when I met him.

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:32.772
-I think just people were paying
less attention to him.

00:04:32.772 --> 00:04:35.341
And then they looked back
in time and were like,

00:04:35.341 --> 00:04:36.009 size:88% position:44% line:92%
"That's a weird choice."

00:04:36.009 --> 00:04:37.644 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, I thought
the beard looked nice.

00:04:37.644 --> 00:04:39.612 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He's getting a lot of heat
for it.

00:04:39.612 --> 00:04:40.313 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I thought it was --

00:04:40.313 --> 00:04:42.415
I mean, we always thought
he was a handsome guy.

00:04:42.415 --> 00:04:43.216 line:92%
-He's getting heat for it?

00:04:43.216 --> 00:04:44.951 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He's getting a lot of heat
for it.

00:04:44.951 --> 00:04:46.919 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, there's not enough
going on.

00:04:46.919 --> 00:04:48.187 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:48.187 --> 00:04:49.589 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think he looks great
with his beard.

00:04:49.589 --> 00:04:51.791
-I agree. I don't even know why
I even brought it up.

00:04:51.791 --> 00:04:54.694 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, I'm going to grow
a little thin mustache.

00:04:54.694 --> 00:04:55.295 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, you are?

00:04:55.295 --> 00:04:56.629 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm inspired by him, yeah.
-Just a real thin one.

00:04:56.629 --> 00:04:59.232 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Just real John Waters thing.
-The John Waters, yeah.

00:04:59.232 --> 00:05:02.201 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, exactly.
[ Laughter ]

